"content_hash":"b9e1ed8b10070640026d3c5f38ef8a4d59ca833d62d36394960970825b71dcbd","event_uuid":"6cd628c0-0ca7-4e8a-a99f-e368b14467ae","position":{"commit_sha":"5a5af443d30dd68a1f6ad95ce18056dcb3f3aa39","position":"1787543284627643001-6cd628c0-0ca7-4e8a-a99f-e368b14467ae"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"199ecd4aa1073d4ca8fb01cce86663a8d4f96654508e91f8b8a54e199178df56","event_uuid":"14844d2a-3285-4694-b3f3-711484df6183","position":{"commit_sha":"b0faed711891986334b78e0d29fca9297fe47144","position":"1787544111234121001-14844d2a-3285-4694-b3f3-711484df6183"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9254fe40a3a057719d806a65eec704584cd464de1fd6e8c9a8a4c52784f9902a","event_uuid":"0d1e7778-e7b6-4b24-9e13-7cb1c6856647","position":{"commit_sha":"01def568f9dd5013cf7190b0c725abbea74d77d0","position":"1787544534305013001-0d1e7778-e7b6-4b24-9e13-7cb1c6856647"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"553914ad8a8bf83507b517024ece4646f9ce3998c669a37f91fa5f87aa607176","event_uuid":"6e4b027e-dd3b-4ae9-9bde-1577cbff2c1c","position":{"commit_sha":"fb9176fa852fe4a157ab867a8e6fcb297f5728b5","position":"1787545051884214001-6e4b027e-dd3b-4ae9-9bde-1577cbff2c1c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"abca370ef82724c4f3bb8fd19737070d285f3675533cd5b4ea03bca0b6021275","event_uuid":"ee4b11fd-901a-46f8-91fb-5ca562d57a9a","position":{"commit_sha":"fb9176fa852fe4a157ab867a8e6fcb297f5728b5","position":"1787545059922261001-ee4b11fd-901a-46f8-91fb-5ca562d57a9a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787543174004595001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6cd628c0-0ca7-4e8a-a99f-e368b14467ae","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4000-2df3-398d-44e2"}],"description":"## Context\nThe duration probe can measure end-to-end close wall time and the verifier workflow, but it currently labels the large interval before the completion verdict as an inferred residual. That attribution is insufficient: a recent normal close was silent for roughly eight minutes, and existing cohorts have much larger gaps. Minimal direct instrumentation is approved only if it cannot exacerbate the performance problem.\n\n## Performance constraint\nInstrumentation must use only `time.monotonic_ns()`, integer arithmetic, and cheap dictionary assignments on the existing call path. It must add no event, tracker write, commit/push, file read, Git command, network call, tracing backend, worker, lock, retry, sleep, or model call. The values must piggyback on the existing `COMPLETION_VERDICT.metrics` payload and its existing sidecar write. A standard-library microbenchmark must show the complete added bookkeeping costs less than 50 microseconds per close, well under 0.01% of a one-minute close, and the command/result must be recorded before landing.\n\n## Plan\n- Start one timing dictionary at `close_ticket` entry. Thread it through the exact existing graph: `close_ticket → _completion_precheck → _check_work_landed → {_referencing_commits → commit_impact.referencing_commits, _check_file_impact_vs_diff}`. Every new argument is optional. Keep `close_precheck._referencing_commits` as the documented monkeypatch/compatibility seam.\n- Record direct milliseconds for `pre_verifier_total_ms`, `structural_scan_ms`, `material_policy_ms`, `descendant_scope_ms`, `landing_check_ms`, `verifier_call_ms`, `git_history_read_ms`, `alias_index_build_ms`, `ticket_ref_resolution_ms`, and `diff_validation_ms`.\n- In `commit_impact.referencing_commits`, time only the already-existing Git-log subprocess wait, alias-index build, and cached reference-resolution loop. Count already-iterated commits, distinct extracted references, and found referencing commits; do not add a second traversal.\n- In `_check_file_impact_vs_diff`, time the existing impact union plus attached/referencing commit changed-path and undeclared-path scan directly inside that function. No work is duplicated for measurement.\n- Resolve the canonical ticket plus transitive descendants once as today, recording the scope time and accepted descendant-id count during the same loop.\n- Measure the existing bounded completion-verifier/auto-resume call. Immediately after it returns, merge the direct fields into its existing `metrics` dictionary before the existing PASS/FAIL sidecar emit, preserving consumption metrics from gate dispatch.\n- Update the reusable duration probe to read the direct fields. Records lacking them are `legacy_uninstrumented`; an unexplained legacy residual is never assigned a causal operation name.\n- Add synthetic RED-first tests for timing propagation, counts, existing-metric preservation, optional-argument compatibility, direct/legacy probe reporting, and unchanged counts of existing subprocess and sidecar calls.\n\n## Timing boundaries\n- `structural_scan_ms`: existing open-child/newly-unblocked batch scan in `close_ticket`.\n- `material_policy_ms`: existing `_plan_review_close_recheck` currency/material policy call.\n- `descendant_scope_ms`: canonical-id resolution plus transitive descendant collection/resolution.\n- `landing_check_ms`: existing `_check_work_landed` call.\n- `verifier_call_ms`: existing `verify_with_auto_resume` call.\n- `pre_verifier_total_ms`: `close_ticket` entry through the instant immediately before `verify_with_auto_resume`.\n- `git_history_read_ms`, `alias_index_build_ms`, and `ticket_ref_resolution_ms`: the named existing sections of `commit_impact.referencing_commits`.\n- `diff_validation_ms`: the existing changed-path/undeclared-path scan inside `_check_file_impact_vs_diff`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A model-backed PASS `COMPLETION_VERDICT` carries all ten direct timing fields.\n- [ ] A model-backed FAIL `COMPLETION_VERDICT` carries all ten direct timing fields.\n- [ ] Existing completion consumption metrics remain present and unchanged.\n- [ ] Sidecar workload counts report commits inspected, distinct references, descendant ids, and referencing commits found.\n- [ ] Instrumentation adds no I/O, subprocess, network call, tracker event/write, or model call.\n- [ ] Instrumentation adds no lock, retry, sleep, tracing backend, or background worker.\n- [ ] Existing callers behave unchanged when no optional timing dictionary is supplied.\n- [ ] The duration probe consumes direct fields when present.\n- [ ] Older probe rows are labeled `legacy_uninstrumented` without a causal label for their residual.\n- [ ] Synthetic tests fail on current main and pass after implementation.\n- [ ] A standard-library microbenchmark measures the complete added bookkeeping below 50 microseconds per close.\n- [ ] Focused tests and the script import walk pass.\n- [ ] Lint, typecheck, and the default non-integration/non-external test suite pass.\n- [ ] Agent-duration guidance remains unchanged pending explicit user confirmation after a post-instrumentation cohort.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"Measure the existing structural and plan-material checks and seed the close timing dictionary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"Measure descendant scope, landing checks, and verifier call; merge direct fields into existing verdict metrics."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py","reason":"Measure the existing Git history read, alias-index build, reference resolution, and workload counts without adding work."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Prefer direct gated-close phase fields and label legacy rows without causal inference."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe_support.py","reason":"Extract the new fields from existing completion sidecar metrics."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_close_duration_instrumentation.py","reason":"Pin timing/count propagation, metric preservation, compatibility, and no-extra-work behavior."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Pin direct-field reporting and legacy_uninstrumented labeling with synthetic fixtures."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6e4b027e-dd3b-4ae9-9bde-1577cbff2c1c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["performance","completion-gate","observability","metrics"],"ticket_id":"3f22-7fd4-aae7-48b4","ticket_type":"task","title":"Emit direct gated-close phase timings in the completion sidecar","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["19ae3301-183c-4813-8c72-048f3d916833","2678b125-20e6-4728-854c-44460dcdb5c4","6cd628c0-0ca7-4e8a-a99f-e368b14467ae","14844d2a-3285-4694-b3f3-711484df6183","0d1e7778-e7b6-4b24-9e13-7cb1c6856647","6e4b027e-dd3b-4ae9-9bde-1577cbff2c1c","ee4b11fd-901a-46f8-91fb-5ca562d57a9a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787548129367067001,"uuid":"1f784f2a-9922-42fc-836d-a830d68fa4fc"}